  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade and Supply Chain Finance Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&apos;s investment in the Asian Development Bank&apos;s Trade and Supply Chain Finance Program supports banks and micro, small and medium sized enterprises in developing countries and least developed countries in the Indo-Pacific to strengthen trade finance capacity and accessibility. Australia&apos;s contribution includes a focus on Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) and Indo-Pacific Economic Framework (IPEF) economies. The Program aims to help close the global trade finance gap by addressing information asymmetries and changing perceptions of risks in the region.</narrative>
  </description>
